<title>INDIA: India Texmaco 1996/97 net surges.</title>
<headline>India Texmaco 1996/97 net surges.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		83.3	 vs	 0.23</p>
<p>    Net sales	    2,844.6	 vs   1,572.1</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	  1.5	 vs	nil</p>
<p>    Other income	    84.8	 vs     131.3</p>
<p>    Expenditure	  2,771.9	 vs   1,633.0</p>
<p>    Interest		  46.7	 vs	51.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    14.4	 vs	12.9</p>
<p>    Tax			 13.2	 vs	 5.4</p>
<p>Note: Calcutta-based Texmaco Ltd said its loss making division, Birla Textile Mills was closed down on November 30, 1996 and is to be relocated in the northern state of Himachal Pradesh.</p>
<p>The firm said all its divisions had fared well except for textile machinery where the company is exploring the possibility of entering into joint venture with some multinationals.</p>
<p>Texmaco said its equity share capital rose to 51.63 million rupees in 1996/97 from 25.82 million in the previous year due to issue of equity shares on rights basis.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
